  "worked_solution": "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=7.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to 7}f(x)$ exists and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {7}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to 7}f(x)=f(7)=13.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {7}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({x}^{2}-f(x)) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({7}^{2}-13) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(36) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({6}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}\u20616.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
